{"index":3252,"node_id":"f504bc3a-af6e-49be-9204-3e2f1dbfb6b6","parent":"5d3ab89a-77bb-418d-baa7-de8db2443030","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791158898.660311,"update_time":1791165893.049656,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Use a single `segmentation` object inside each file’s existing `metadata` object.\n\nThe important design choice is that **all positional coordinates should be relative to the document body, excluding the metadata line itself**. Otherwise, changing metadata changes every downstream character offset.\n\nI would use this contract:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"this\": \"metadata\",\n    \"file_description\": \"...\",\n    \"segmentation\": {\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"coordinate_space\": \"body\",\n      \"segments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"segment-1\",\n          \"mode\": \"static\",\n          \"start\": 0,\n          \"end\": 420\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"segment-2\",\n          \"mode\": \"dynamic\",\n          \"start_marker\": \"## Inputs\",\n          \"end_marker\": \"## Outputs\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nFor **static** segments, `start` and `end` are body-relative character offsets. For **dynamic** segments, the segment is located from stable markers rather than offsets.\n\nI would also have the updater resolve every segment before writing and maintain a derived position record:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"segment-2\",\n  \"mode\": \"dynamic\",\n  \"start_marker\": \"## Inputs\",\n  \"end_marker\": \"## Outputs\",\n  \"resolved_start\": 421,\n  \"resolved_end\": 812\n}\n```\n\nThat gives you both:\n\n- the **authoritative locator** — static offsets or dynamic markers;\n- the **currently resolved location** — useful for deterministic subsequent operations.\n\nThen an update operation can eventually look like:\n\n```yaml\n- name: update-segment\n  script: update-functions/update-segment.js\n  args:\n    - - 10 Inputs/10 Inputs.txt\n      - segment-2\n      - replacement text\n```\n\nand the function can:\n\n```text\nread metadata\n→ identify segment by id\n→ resolve current boundaries\n→ replace only that segment\n→ recompute tracked segment positions\n→ rewrite metadata\n```\n\nI would make `id` permanent. The segment's location may change; its identity should not."}
{"index":3253,"node_id":"bbb21242-a43b-4d79-b1bf-f27202856de8","parent":"f504bc3a-af6e-49be-9204-3e2f1dbfb6b6","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791159122.356925,"update_time":1791159483.432939,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"In that case reserve an area for the metadata using as recurring character non space"}
{"index":3254,"node_id":"0cb37ac4-2a0e-4e1a-8e67-5e18666fa0e2","parent":"bbb21242-a43b-4d79-b1bf-f27202856de8","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791159132.753783,"update_time":1791159139.035861,"content_type":"thoughts","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"thoughts\",\"thoughts\":[{\"summary\":\"Planning metadata space\",\"content\":\"I’m interpreting this as a fixed-width metadata region padded with a recurring non-space character, so changing metadata won’t shift the main content. I need the intended capacity and filler character before choosing a robust implementation.\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true},{\"summary\":\"Planned metadata space\",\"content\":\"\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true}],\"source_analysis_msg_id\":\"173203e8-386b-4e49-839d-114bdd240563\"}"}
{"index":3255,"node_id":"3cd57c2e-690f-4e86-876c-8bfebc0170b6","parent":"0cb37ac4-2a0e-4e1a-8e67-5e18666fa0e2","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791159148.550136,"update_time":1791159150.65538,"content_type":"thoughts","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"thoughts\",\"thoughts\":[{\"summary\":\"Designing fixed offsets\",\"content\":\"I’m using a fixed-size metadata block: one JSON line, a newline, then repeated `~` padding until the reserved length. The body begins at the same offset, provided metadata stays within capacity.\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true},{\"summary\":\"Designed fixed offsets\",\"content\":\"\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true}],\"source_analysis_msg_id\":\"a2e5a376-8183-4d8c-8e2f-9d16cdd1a02a\"}"}
